---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { loadTimeline } from "../lib/timeline";

const { profile } = loadTimeline();
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  description={`What ${profile.name}'s site collects, and what it doesn't: no cookies, no accounts, no tracking across sites.`}
  effective="2026-10-22"
>
  <p>
    This is a personal site. It has no accounts, no forms, no cookies and no advertising, and it never sells or shares
    anything about you. This page explains the little that does happen when you visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {profile.name}, {profile.location}. Questions or requests go to <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}
      >{profile.email}</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a set of static files served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare receives the technical details
    every browser sends with a request (your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the referring page) and
    uses them to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Cloudflare handles that data under the <a
      href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
      rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a
    >. The site itself runs no server code and stores none of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits. It sets no cookies, does not use local storage, and does not
    fingerprint you or follow you to other sites. It reports aggregate figures such as page views, referring sites,
    browser and device type, country, and page load times. The script loads from <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code
    >, and a content blocker that stops it does not change anything about the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The observations you earn by exploring are saved in your browser's local storage under the key <code
      >ianpascoe.observations.v1</code
    >: which observations you logged and when. That record never leaves your device; it is not sent to the site,
    Cloudflare or anyone else. Clearing this site's data in your browser erases it.
  </p>

  <h2>Clipboard</h2>
  <p>
    The "Copy address" button writes the email address to your clipboard when you press it. The site never reads your
    clipboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to {profile.email}, Cloudflare Email Routing forwards your message to {profile.name.split(" ")[0]}'s
    personal Google (Gmail) mailbox. Your name, address and whatever you write are kept there so the conversation can
    continue, and are used only to reply to you. Ask and they will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts and other services</h2>
  <p>
    Fonts and images are served from this site, not from third-party font or image services. Links to GitHub, LinkedIn,
    X and other sites take you to services with their own privacy policies; nothing about your visit is passed to them
    beyond what your browser sends when you follow a link.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Block the analytics script or use your browser's privacy features; the site works the same.</li>
    <li>Clear this site's data to erase your observations.</li>
    <li>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> to ask what correspondence is held about you, to correct
      it, or to have it deleted.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The site is meant for a professional audience and does not knowingly collect anything from children.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new effective date. The history of every change is
    public in the site's <a href="https://github.com/ian-pascoe/ian-pascoe" rel="noopener">source repository</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
